  "text": "In May of 2020 we returned to \"the paycheck protection program\" — 36 of us at the peak, on a single day. 32 of us said \"back to work.\" \"The cares act\" drew 28 of us; \"health and economic\" drew another 28. When we issued a \"statement after voting,\" 30 of us reached for those same three words. Toward the end of the month the language narrowed to a bill: \"protection program flexibility act,\" 27 of us, and its longer form, \"paycheck protection program flexibility act,\" 26. And 26 of us described what had happened \"behind closed doors.\" We record this without comment. In one month, across these eight phrases, we said the same things in the same order, and the count of us saying each can be read here.",
